  "title": "Convert `deepFreeze` `Memo` from a type to a class",
  "body": "## Changelog Entry\n\nNone. This is an internal refactor of an unreleased package, so it should get the `no-changelog` label.\n\n## Description\n\nFollow-up to #6053. In `packages/store/src/private/deepFreeze.ts`, `Memo` is now a class instead of a plain object type with two free helper functions. Behavior is unchanged.\n\n> This branch is stacked on `feat-new-store` (#6053). It should target that branch, or be rebased after #6053 merges.\n\n## Design\n\n`Memo` now owns both of its stacks and the lookup through private fields. Before this change, `deepFreezeWithMemo()` read `memo.values` and `memo.frozenValues` directly and checked the `IN_PROGRESS` marker itself. That logic is now inside the class.\n\n`get()` returns `undefined` when the value is not an ancestor. A real ancestor never maps to a falsy value: it maps to either a frozen object/array or `IN_PROGRESS`. So a truthy check at the call site is enough.\n\n```ts\nconst ancestorFrozenValue = memo.get(value); // throws on a recursive Set\n\nif (ancestorFrozenValue) {\n  return ancestorFrozenValue;\n}\n```\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- **`Memo` class**\n   - Uses the private fields `#frozenValues` and `#values`. Linear search over arrays is kept.\n   - `push(value, frozenValue)` / `pop()` replace `pushAncestor()` / `popAncestor()`.\n   - `get(value)` returns the ancestor's frozen value, or `undefined` if the value is not an ancestor. It still throws `TypeError('Recursive Set cannot be frozen')` when the ancestor is a `Set` that is still being frozen.\n- **Call sites**\n   - `deepFreezeArray()`, `deepFreezeObject()`, and the `Set` branch of `deepFreezeWithMemo()` call `memo.push()` / `memo.pop()`.\n   - `deepFreeze()` creates the memo with `new Memo()`.\n\n- [ ] ~I have added tests and executed them locally~ (existing `deepFreeze` tests cover this; no new behavior)\n- [ ] ~I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`~\n- [ ] ~I have updated documentation~\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] ~Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)~\n- [ ] ~Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed~\n- [ ] ~CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)~\n- [ ] ~Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)~\n- [ ] ~Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)~\n- [ ] ~`package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed~\n- [ ] ~Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)~\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)",
